nodecode-speech is a rewrite of allmodels-io's allmodels-io/hermes-speech:

  https://github.com/allmodels-io/hermes-speech
  commit 6efecc359aa4c091b41ad530575943657ee259de
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 AllModels (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the AllModels client and the call paths behind it -- the API root
and its /oai OpenAI-compatible base (client.py), the bearer key that is either
inline or read from the variable api_key_env names (client.py's API_KEY_ENV and
get_api_key), text-to-speech as POST {root}/oai/v1/audio/speech with the model,
voice, input, response_format, speed and provider fields, the x-idempotency-key
header, the 0.25 to 4.0 speed clamp and the mp3/opus/aac/flac/wav/pcm response
formats (providers.py's AllModelsTTSProvider.synthesize), speech-to-text as one
multipart POST {root}/oai/v1/audio/transcriptions with the model, file,
language and prompt (providers.py's AllModelsTranscriptionProvider.transcribe),
and the public, cursor-paginated voice catalogue at GET /v1/voices with its q,
model, provider, language and page_size parameters, flattened per voice and
provider the way catalog.py's _normalize_voice_entry did (client.py's
list_voices). The per-profile speech settings the plugin wrote into Hermes'
config.yaml -- tts.model, tts.voice, tts.allmodels.voice_provider, tts.speed,
tts.output_format, stt.allmodels.model, language and prompt -- are the cell's
allmodels-speech config section, read by the same three verbs the plugin's
providers served.

Left out: the Hermes-only surfaces -- registration as Hermes' own TTS and
transcription provider, the sentence-pipelined voice mode and the streaming
PCM path (streaming.py), the Ogg/Opus switch for messaging gateways, MEDIA:
delivery, the /voice pipeline, the two bundled skills and the setup and
management tools that drove them, the email signup and verification flow, the
background model-catalogue cache, and the GitHub release update checker --
because they plug into Hermes' runtime or its UI rather than describe an API,
and a cell reaches AllModels directly through nlk:http instead. Signup,
top-up links and the model catalogue are therefore not in the rewrite: a user
brings a key from allmodels.io, and /speech balance reads the account's credit
the way the plugin's own balance command did.
